and the Family Law</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://family.jrank.org/pages/1741/Vietnam-Gender-Equity-Marriage-Family-Law-1959.html"/></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bunck</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Women and post-cold war socialism: the cases of Cuba and Vietnam</article-title><source>Cuba in transition: papers and proceedings of the seventh annual meeting of the association for the study of the Cuban economy: 1997</source><year>1997</year><publisher-name>ASCE</publisher-name><fpage>31</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chuc</surname><given-names>NTK</given-names></name><name><surname>Diwan</surname><given-names>VK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Filabavi: a demographic surveillance site, an epidemiological field laboratory in Vietnam</article-title><source>Scandinavian Journal of Public Health</source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>3</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14578073</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1080/14034950310015031</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organisation</collab></person-group><source>Putting women first Guidelines on ethics and safety for violence research</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>Geneva: WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>World Health Organisation</collab></person-group><source>WHO Multi-country study of Women's health and domestic violence</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>Core protocol WHO/EIP/GPE/99.3 Geneva: WHO</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-ty